# House style

Edit this file to change how the bot builds. It is read fresh on every `!make`,
so save the file and the next build obeys it - no restart, no code. Everything
below is sent to the planner as standing instructions that override its general
guidance. Delete anything you disagree with.

Keep it short. Long lists of rules dilute each other; a dozen sharp lines beat
three pages. There is an 8000 character cap.

## Materials

- Prefer deepslate_bricks, stone_bricks and polished_andesite for stonework.
  Avoid plain cobblestone as a main wall material - use it for plinths and trim.
- Wood: spruce_planks and stripped_oak_log. Avoid oak_planks as a large surface.
- Roofs: deepslate_tiles, dark_oak_planks or blue_terracotta. Never the same
  block as the walls.

## Proportions

- A tower reads best at 4 to 6 times its own width in height.
- A doorway is 2 wide and 3 tall. Windows are no wider than 2.
- Anything over 12 blocks tall gets a trim band every 5 or 6 levels.

## Always

- A plinth one block wider than the building, in a darker block.
- Eaves under every roof: upside-down stairs, one block proud of the wall.
- Windows are glazed with glass_pane, never left as holes.
- At least one light source visible from outside after dark.

## Never

- A flat slab roof.
- A building whose walls are a single material with no banding or trim.
- A wall longer than 10 blocks with nothing on it.
